2026-09-04T06:13Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context
Found incidentally while running `make check` on an unrelated branch
(ticket 0639, 2026-09-04): `bench/check_ticket_logs.py` fails on `origin/main`
as of `a947e71` (the commit that closed and archived 0635):

    FAIL: tickets/closed/0635-tmpdir-xdg-home-redirection-for-zoteus-s.erg:10:
    stamped 2026-09-04T06:10Z, written 2026-09-04T05:40Z
    1 log entry is stamped after the commit that wrote it.

This is pre-existing on `main`, not introduced by this ticket's own work, and
blocks `make check`/`make lint`'s `ticket-logs` target for every branch until
fixed.

## Relevant files
- `tickets/closed/0635-tmpdir-xdg-home-redirection-for-zoteus-s.erg:10` — the
  drifted stamp
- `bench/check_ticket_logs.py` — the gate that caught it

## Actions
1. Find the commit that actually introduced line 10 (`git log -L 10,10:tickets/closed/0635-...erg` or equivalent) and read its real timestamp.
2. Correct the stamp on that line to the time the commit evidences, per
   `rules/workflow.md`'s general instruction: "Correct the stamp to a time
   the record evidences … never the other way round."

## Verification
- [ ] `python3 bench/check_ticket_logs.py` passes on `main` after the fix

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `make check`'s `ticket-logs` target is green on `main`
